IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nt-claims-dates`

-- Native Title Act 1993 (Cth) -- the questions of a member of a native title claim group (or compensation claim group)
-- who brings a claim: who may apply (s 61, s 251B) and what may not be claimed (s 61A); earlier extinguishment that is
-- disregarded (ss 47, 47A, 47B); registration of the claim (ss 190A-190C) and what follows a refusal (ss 190D-190F);
-- becoming a party to someone else's application (ss 66(10)(c), 84); replacing the applicant (s 66B); the right to
-- negotiate over a proposed act (ss 29-32, 35-38, 41); and compensation (ss 49-51A, 53, with s 61(1)).
--
-- SEAT: a member of the native title claim group, or of the compensation claim group, including the person or persons
-- the group authorises to be the applicant. "Can we apply?", "Will our claim be registered?", "By when must I ...?",
-- "Are we a native title party?", "Can the act go ahead without negotiating with us?", "What compensation can we get?".
-- The Federal Court, the Native Title Registrar, the National Native Title Tribunal (NNTT), the arbitral body and the
-- Ministers get no seat: their satisfactions and opinions are asked as facts.
--
-- Every exported question takes plain facts (yes/no, a number, a date). No question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT. The
-- duties with deadlines the person meets are regulative rules run by EVALTRACE inside questions: s 66(10)(c) with
-- s 84(3)(b) (notify the Federal Court within 3 months starting on the notification day), s 30(1)(a)(i) (file the
-- claimant application before the end of 3 months after the notification day) and s 190E(2)(b) (apply to the NNTT for
-- reconsideration within 42 days after the s 190D(1) notice).
--
-- Edition: Native Title Act 1993, compilation register id C2024C00224, deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A04665.txt (retrieved 13 October 2026).
--
-- Sourced from the Federal Register of Legislation, Commonwealth of Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. Answers follow the rulings on negatives of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05
-- (NOTES.md): an answer that is the text's own no is marked "(the text's no)"; an answer where the text is limited by its
-- own wording or silent is marked "NOTHING-kind".

§ `Native Title Act 1993: the questions of a member of a claim group`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `the condition` IS A BOOLEAN, `the label` IS A STRING, `the rest` IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`if` `the condition` `add` `the label` `to` `the rest` MEANS
    IF `the condition` THEN `the label` FOLLOWED BY `the rest` ELSE `the rest`

§§ `s 251B -- Is the applicant authorised by all the persons in the claim group?`

-- s 251B: "all the persons in a native title claim group or compensation claim group authorise a person or persons to
-- make a native title determination application or a compensation application, and to deal with matters arising in
-- relation to it, if: (a) where there is a process of decision-making that, under the traditional laws and customs of
-- the persons in the ... group, must be complied with in relation to authorising things of that kind--the persons ...
-- authorise the person or persons ... in accordance with that process; or (b) where there is no such process--the
-- persons ... authorise the other person or persons ... in accordance with a process of decision-making agreed to and
-- adopted, by the persons in the ... group". A definition ("authorise ... if") with "where" limbs: the text's no when the
-- limb that applies is not met (ruling (b) of 2026-11-05).
GIVEN `a traditional process must be followed` IS A BOOLEAN, `authorised by the traditional process` IS A BOOLEAN, `authorised by an agreed and adopted process` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 251B -- the applicant is authorised by all the persons in the group` `a traditional process must be followed` `authorised by the traditional process` `authorised by an agreed and adopted process` IF
    IF `a traditional process must be followed`
    THEN `authorised by the traditional process`
    ELSE `authorised by an agreed and adopted process`

§§ `s 61A -- What may a claimant application not cover or claim?`

-- s 61A(1): "A native title determination application must not be made in relation to an area for which there is an
-- approved determination of native title."
-- s 61A(2): if a previous exclusive possession act (s 23B) was done in relation to an area, and it was attributable to
-- the Commonwealth, or to a State or Territory whose law has made provision as mentioned in s 23E, "a claimant
-- application must not be made that covers any of the area".
-- s 61A(3): for a previous non-exclusive possession act (s 23F) on the same terms (s 23I), "a claimant application must
-- not be made in which any of the native title rights and interests claimed confer possession, occupation, use and
-- enjoyment of any of the area to the exclusion of all others".
-- s 61A(4): (2) and (3) do not apply if the only such act is one whose extinguishment ss 47, 47A, 47B or 47C would require
-- to be disregarded, and the application states that the section applies. Whether an act is a previous exclusive or
-- non-exclusive possession act (ss 23B, 23F) and whether the State law has made the s 23E or 23I provision are asked as
-- facts (fork F2).
DECLARE `What s 61A says about our application` IS ONE OF
    `s 61A does not stop it`
    `no: there is an approved determination of native title for the area (s 61A(1), the text's no)`
    `no: it must not cover any of an area where a previous exclusive possession act was done (s 61A(2), the text's no); leave that area out, or, if ss 47, 47A, 47B or 47C require that extinguishment to be disregarded, say so in the application (s 61A(4))`
    `not as framed: it must not claim possession, occupation, use and enjoyment to the exclusion of all others over an area where a previous non-exclusive possession act was done (s 61A(3), the text's no); claim non-exclusive rights there, or rely on ss 47-47C and say so (s 61A(4))`

GIVEN `there is an approved determination for the area` IS A BOOLEAN, `a previous exclusive possession act covers any of the area` IS A BOOLEAN, `a previous non-exclusive possession act covers any of the area` IS A BOOLEAN, `we claim exclusive possession of that area` IS A BOOLEAN, `ss 47 to 47C disregard those acts and the application says so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What s 61A says about our application`
`s 61A -- what it says about our application` `there is an approved determination for the area` `a previous exclusive possession act covers any of the area` `a previous non-exclusive possession act covers any of the area` `we claim exclusive possession of that area` `ss 47 to 47C disregard those acts and the application says so` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `there is an approved determination for the area`
        THEN `no: there is an approved determination of native title for the area (s 61A(1), the text's no)`
        IF `ss 47 to 47C disregard those acts and the application says so`
        THEN `s 61A does not stop it`
        IF `a previous exclusive possession act covers any of the area`
        THEN `no: it must not cover any of an area where a previous exclusive possession act was done (s 61A(2), the text's no); leave that area out, or, if ss 47, 47A, 47B or 47C require that extinguishment to be disregarded, say so in the application (s 61A(4))`
        IF `a previous non-exclusive possession act covers any of the area` AND `we claim exclusive possession of that area`
        THEN `not as framed: it must not claim possession, occupation, use and enjoyment to the exclusion of all others over an area where a previous non-exclusive possession act was done (s 61A(3), the text's no); claim non-exclusive rights there, or rely on ss 47-47C and say so (s 61A(4))`
        OTHERWISE `s 61A does not stop it`

§§ `s 61 -- Can we make a native title determination application?`

-- s 61(1), table, "Native title determination application", persons who may make it: "(1) A person or persons authorised
-- by all the persons (the native title claim group) who, according to their traditional laws and customs, hold the
-- common or group rights and interests comprising the particular native title claimed, provided the person or persons
-- are also included in the native title claim group". The other persons in the table (a non-native title interest
-- holder, the Ministers) are not in this seat. s 61(2): the authorised person is, or the persons are jointly, the
-- applicant, and no other member of the group is. The table is read as closing the list of who may apply (fork F3).
DECLARE `Can we make a native title determination application` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the person or persons the group authorised may apply to the Federal Court, and will jointly be the applicant (s 61(1), (2)); the application must meet ss 61(3)-(5) and 62`
    `no: the person who applies must also be included in the native title claim group (s 61(1), the text's no)`
    `no: the applicant must be authorised by all the persons in the native title claim group, in the way s 251B requires (s 61(1), s 251B, the text's no)`
    `no: s 61A forbids this application` HAS `the reason` IS A `What s 61A says about our application`

@export Can the person our native title claim group has chosen make a native title determination application to the Federal Court for our area (Native Title Act 1993 ss 61, 61A, 251B)? The person must be in the group and authorised by all of it, and the application must not cover an area with an approved determination or (unless ss 47-47C apply) a previous exclusive possession act.
GIVEN `the applicant is in the claim group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person (or each of the persons) who will make the application is a member of the native title claim group
      `a traditional process must be followed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, under your group's traditional laws and customs, there is a process of decision-making that must be followed to authorise things of this kind
      `authorised by the traditional process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is such a traditional process, whether the group authorised the applicant to make the application and deal with matters arising under it in accordance with that process
      `authorised by an agreed and adopted process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is no such traditional process, whether the group authorised the applicant under a decision-making process the group agreed to and adopted
      `there is an approved determination for the area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is already an approved determination of native title (that native title exists or does not) for any of the area
      `a previous exclusive possession act covers any of the area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a previous exclusive possession act (for example a grant of freehold or certain leases before 23 December 1996) was done over any of the area and is attributable to the Commonwealth, or to a State or Territory whose law has confirmed its effect (s 23E)
      `a previous non-exclusive possession act covers any of the area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a previous non-exclusive possession act (for example a pastoral lease) was done over any of the area and is attributable to the Commonwealth, or to a State or Territory whose law has confirmed its effect (s 23I)
      `we claim exclusive possession of that area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application claims possession, occupation, use and enjoyment to the exclusion of all others over the area of the previous non-exclusive possession act
      `ss 47 to 47C disregard those acts and the application says so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only such acts are ones whose extinguishment ss 47, 47A, 47B or 47C require to be disregarded, and the application states that the section applies
GIVETH A `Can we make a native title determination application`
`s 61 -- can we make a native title determination application` `the applicant is in the claim group` `a traditional process must be followed` `authorised by the traditional process` `authorised by an agreed and adopted process` `there is an approved determination for the area` `a previous exclusive possession act covers any of the area` `a previous non-exclusive possession act covers any of the area` `we claim exclusive possession of that area` `ss 47 to 47C disregard those acts and the application says so` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the applicant is in the claim group`)
        THEN `no: the person who applies must also be included in the native title claim group (s 61(1), the text's no)`
        IF (NOT (`s 251B -- the applicant is authorised by all the persons in the group` `a traditional process must be followed` `authorised by the traditional process` `authorised by an agreed and adopted process`))
        THEN `no: the applicant must be authorised by all the persons in the native title claim group, in the way s 251B requires (s 61(1), s 251B, the text's no)`
        IF `the s 61A answer` EQUALS `s 61A does not stop it`
        THEN `yes: the person or persons the group authorised may apply to the Federal Court, and will jointly be the applicant (s 61(1), (2)); the application must meet ss 61(3)-(5) and 62`
        OTHERWISE `no: s 61A forbids this application` `the s 61A answer`
    WHERE
        `the s 61A answer` MEANS `s 61A -- what it says about our application` `there is an approved determination for the area` `a previous exclusive possession act covers any of the area` `a previous non-exclusive possession act covers any of the area` `we claim exclusive possession of that area` `ss 47 to 47C disregard those acts and the application says so`

§§ `ss 47, 47A, 47B -- Is earlier extinguishment over our area disregarded?`

-- s 47(1): applies if an application under s 61 is made and, when it is made, "a pastoral lease is held over the area by:
-- (i) any of the persons who made the application claiming to hold the native title or any other persons with whom they
-- claimed to hold the title; or (ii) a trustee, on trust for any of those persons; or (iii) a company whose only
-- shareholders or ... members are any of those persons". (2): any extinguishment by the grant of the lease, the creation
-- of any other interest, or acts under the lease "must be disregarded".
-- s 47A(1): a claimant application, and when it is made (b)(i) a freehold estate, lease or vesting under legislation
-- that provides for such grants "only to, in or for the benefit of, Aboriginal peoples or Torres Strait Islanders", or
-- (ii) the area is held or reserved expressly for their benefit; and (c) one or more members of the claim group occupy
-- the area. (2): extinguishment by that grant or vesting, and by any other prior interest (other than, for (b)(ii), a
-- freehold grant for services), is disregarded.
-- s 47B(1): a claimant application, and when it is made the area is not (i) covered by a freehold estate or lease,
-- (ii) covered by a reservation, proclamation, dedication etc. for public purposes or a particular purpose, or (iii)
-- subject to a resumption process; and (c) one or more members of the group occupy the area. (2): extinguishment by the
-- creation of any prior interest is disregarded.
-- Each section "applies if": when its conditions fail, that section does not apply (the text's no). s 47C (park areas,
-- by written agreement with the government) is not encoded (NOTES.md). The note to each: "The applicant will still need
-- to show the existence of any connection with the land or waters concerned that may be required by the common law".
DECLARE `Is earlier extinguishment disregarded` IS ONE OF
    `yes, under s 47: the extinguishment by the pastoral lease, any other interest, and acts under it is disregarded for all purposes of the application (s 47(2)); you must still show connection`
    `yes, under s 47A: the extinguishment by the grant, vesting, holding or reservation for Aboriginal peoples or Torres Strait Islanders, and by other prior interests, is disregarded (s 47A(2)); you must still show connection`
    `yes, under s 47B: the extinguishment by the creation of any prior interest in this vacant Crown land is disregarded (s 47B(2)); you must still show connection`
    `not under ss 47, 47A or 47B on these facts: each applies only if its conditions hold (the text's no); s 47C (park areas, by agreement) is not encoded here`

@export Is earlier extinguishment of native title over the area we claim disregarded, because we hold the pastoral lease, the land is Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander land we occupy, or it is vacant Crown land we occupy (Native Title Act 1993 ss 47, 47A, 47B)?
GIVEN `a pastoral lease is held by claimants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the application was made, a pastoral lease over the area was held by any of the claimants (or the people they claim with), by a trustee for any of them, or by a company whose only shareholders or members are any of them
      `the area is held for Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander peoples` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the application was made, the area was freehold, leased or vested under legislation that allows such grants only to or for Aboriginal peoples or Torres Strait Islanders, or was held, held on trust or reserved expressly for their benefit
      `the area is vacant Crown land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the application was made, the area was not covered by any freehold or lease, not reserved, proclaimed or dedicated for a public or particular purpose, and not subject to a resumption process
      `a member of our group occupies the area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the application was made, one or more members of the native title claim group occupied the area
GIVETH AN `Is earlier extinguishment disregarded`
`ss 47-47B -- is earlier extinguishment disregarded` `a pastoral lease is held by claimants` `the area is held for Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander peoples` `the area is vacant Crown land` `a member of our group occupies the area` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a pastoral lease is held by claimants`
        THEN `yes, under s 47: the extinguishment by the pastoral lease, any other interest, and acts under it is disregarded for all purposes of the application (s 47(2)); you must still show connection`
        IF `the area is held for Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander peoples` AND `a member of our group occupies the area`
        THEN `yes, under s 47A: the extinguishment by the grant, vesting, holding or reservation for Aboriginal peoples or Torres Strait Islanders, and by other prior interests, is disregarded (s 47A(2)); you must still show connection`
        IF `the area is vacant Crown land` AND `a member of our group occupies the area`
        THEN `yes, under s 47B: the extinguishment by the creation of any prior interest in this vacant Crown land is disregarded (s 47B(2)); you must still show connection`
        OTHERWISE `not under ss 47, 47A or 47B on these facts: each applies only if its conditions hold (the text's no); s 47C (park areas, by agreement) is not encoded here`

§§ `ss 190A-190C -- Will the Registrar accept our claim for registration?`

-- s 190A(6): "The Registrar must accept the claim for registration if: (a) either: (i) the claim was made in an
-- application given to the Registrar under section 63; or (ii) the claim was made in an amended application given to the
-- Registrar under subsection 64(4) and subsection (6A) of this section does not apply; and (b) the claim satisfies all of
-- the conditions in: (i) section 190B ...; and (ii) section 190C".
-- s 190A(6A): an amended claim must be accepted if the earlier claim was accepted and the Registrar is satisfied that the
-- only effect of the amendment is one of the listed kinds (reducing the area, removing a right claimed, giving effect to
-- s 47C, a change of representative body name, a change of address for service).
-- s 190A(6B): "If neither subsection (6) nor (6A) applies, the Registrar must not accept the claim for registration."
-- (the text's no).
-- s 190B: (2) area identified with reasonable certainty; (3) group named or described sufficiently clearly; (4) rights
-- readily identified; (5) factual basis sufficient (association; traditional laws and customs; continued holding);
-- (6) prima facie at least some rights can be established; (7) at least one member has or had a traditional physical
-- connection, or would have but for things done by the Crown, a statutory authority or a leaseholder; (8) the
-- application must not disclose that s 61A forbade it; (9) it must not disclose that (a) the minerals, petroleum or gas
-- claimed are wholly owned by the Crown, (b) offshore rights claimed exclude all others, or (c) the rights were otherwise
-- extinguished (except as ss 47-47C require to be disregarded).
-- s 190C: (2) all details and the affidavit required by ss 61 and 62; (3) no member of the group was in the group for a
-- previous overlapping application whose claim was on the Register when this one was made, as a result of s 190A
-- consideration; (4) certified by each representative body that could certify it, or (4AA) the applicant is a member
-- authorised by all the others and any s 251BA conditions are satisfied, with (5) the application saying so and briefly
-- giving the grounds.
-- Each satisfaction of the Registrar is an input. The Registrar's opinion is the deciding one: the person states what
-- the Registrar was (or would be) satisfied of.
DECLARE `Will our claim be registered` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Registrar must accept the claim, as it meets every condition in ss 190B and 190C (s 190A(6))`
    `yes: the Registrar must accept the amended claim, since the earlier claim was accepted and the amendment only does one of the things s 190A(6A) lists`
    `no: the Registrar must not accept the claim (s 190A(6B), the text's no); you will be given reasons (s 190D) and may seek reconsideration by the NNTT (s 190E) or review by the Federal Court (s 190F)` HAS `the conditions not met` IS A LIST OF STRING

@export Will the Native Title Registrar accept our native title claim for registration on the Register of Native Title Claims (Native Title Act 1993 ss 190A, 190B, 190C)? If not, which of the conditions are not met?
GIVEN `this is an amended application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is in an amended application (rather than the application as first given to the Registrar)
      `the earlier claim was accepted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an amended application, whether the Registrar accepted the claim in the earlier application for registration
      `the amendment only reduces the area or removes rights or updates details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an amended application, whether the Registrar is satisfied that the only effect of the amendment is to reduce the area (with the area still identifiable), remove a claimed right, give effect to s 47C, update the representative body's name, or change the address for service
      `the area is identified with reasonable certainty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied that the description and map let it be said with reasonable certainty which land and waters are claimed (s 190B(2))
      `the group is named or clearly described` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied that the members of the claim group are named, or described clearly enough to tell whether a particular person is in it (s 190B(3))
      `the rights claimed are readily identified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied that the description of the native title rights and interests claimed lets them be readily identified (s 190B(4))
      `the factual basis is sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied the factual basis supports association with the area, traditional laws and customs giving rise to the claim, and continued holding under them (s 190B(5))
      `some rights can be established prima facie` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar considers that, prima facie, at least some of the rights claimed can be established (s 190B(6))
      `a member has a traditional physical connection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied at least one member has or had a traditional physical connection with part of the area, or would have but for things done by the Crown, a statutory authority or a leaseholder (s 190B(7))
      `s 61A forbade the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application or the Registrar's information shows that s 61A forbade making it (an approved determination, or a previous possession act not disregarded) (s 190B(8))
      `the Crown wholly owns minerals claimed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim includes ownership of minerals, petroleum or gas that the Crown wholly owns (s 190B(9)(a))
      `exclusive rights are claimed offshore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim purports to exclude all other rights in an offshore place (s 190B(9)(b))
      `the rights claimed were otherwise extinguished` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application or the Registrar's information shows the rights claimed were otherwise extinguished, other than extinguishment ss 47-47C require to be disregarded (s 190B(9)(c))
      `the application has everything ss 61 and 62 require` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar is satisfied the application contains all the details and the affidavit ss 61 and 62 require (s 190C(2))
      `a member was in an earlier registered overlapping claim group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any member of your group was in the group for an earlier application over any of the same area whose claim was on the Register (after the Registrar's consideration) when your application was made (s 190C(3))
      `certified by every representative body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application was certified by each representative Aboriginal/Torres Strait Islander body that could certify it (s 190C(4)(a))
      `the applicant is a member authorised by all the others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant is a member of the group and authorised by all the other members to make the application and deal with matters under it (s 190C(4AA)(a))
      `any conditions on the authority are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there are no s 251BA conditions on the authority to make the application, or all such conditions have been satisfied (s 190C(4AA)(b))
      `the application states and grounds the authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an uncertified application, whether it states that the applicant is a member authorised by all the others (with conditions met) and briefly sets out the grounds (s 190C(5))
GIVETH A `Will our claim be registered`
`ss 190A-190C -- will our claim be registered` `this is an amended application` `the earlier claim was accepted` `the amendment only reduces the area or removes rights or updates details` `the area is identified with reasonable certainty` `the group is named or clearly described` `the rights claimed are readily identified` `the factual basis is sufficient` `some rights can be established prima facie` `a member has a traditional physical connection` `s 61A forbade the application` `the Crown wholly owns minerals claimed` `exclusive rights are claimed offshore` `the rights claimed were otherwise extinguished` `the application has everything ss 61 and 62 require` `a member was in an earlier registered overlapping claim group` `certified by every representative body` `the applicant is a member authorised by all the others` `any conditions on the authority are satisfied` `the application states and grounds the authorisation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `this is an amended application` AND `the earlier claim was accepted` AND `the amendment only reduces the area or removes rights or updates details`
        THEN `yes: the Registrar must accept the amended claim, since the earlier claim was accepted and the amendment only does one of the things s 190A(6A) lists`
        IF `the failures` EQUALS EMPTY
        THEN `yes: the Registrar must accept the claim, as it meets every condition in ss 190B and 190C (s 190A(6))`
        OTHERWISE `no: the Registrar must not accept the claim (s 190A(6B), the text's no); you will be given reasons (s 190D) and may seek reconsideration by the NNTT (s 190E) or review by the Federal Court (s 190F)` `the failures`
    WHERE
        `the s 190C(4) condition is met` MEANS
                `certified by every representative body`
            OR  (    `the applicant is a member authorised by all the others`
                 AND `any conditions on the authority are satisfied`
                 AND `the application states and grounds the authorisation`)
        `the failures` MEANS
            `if` (NOT `the area is identified with reasonable certainty`) `add` "s 190B(2): area not identified with reasonable certainty" `to` (
            `if` (NOT `the group is named or clearly described`) `add` "s 190B(3): claim group not named or clearly described" `to` (
            `if` (NOT `the rights claimed are readily identified`) `add` "s 190B(4): rights claimed not readily identified" `to` (
            `if` (NOT `the factual basis is sufficient`) `add` "s 190B(5): factual basis not sufficient" `to` (
            `if` (NOT `some rights can be established prima facie`) `add` "s 190B(6): no right claimed can be established prima facie" `to` (
            `if` (NOT `a member has a traditional physical connection`) `add` "s 190B(7): no traditional physical connection shown" `to` (
            `if` `s 61A forbade the application` `add` "s 190B(8): s 61A forbade the application" `to` (
            `if` `the Crown wholly owns minerals claimed` `add` "s 190B(9)(a): minerals, petroleum or gas claimed are wholly owned by the Crown" `to` (
            `if` `exclusive rights are claimed offshore` `add` "s 190B(9)(b): exclusive rights claimed in an offshore place" `to` (
            `if` `the rights claimed were otherwise extinguished` `add` "s 190B(9)(c): rights claimed otherwise extinguished" `to` (
            `if` (NOT `the application has everything ss 61 and 62 require`) `add` "s 190C(2): details or affidavit required by ss 61 and 62 missing" `to` (
            `if` `a member was in an earlier registered overlapping claim group` `add` "s 190C(3): a member was in an earlier registered overlapping claim group" `to` (
            `if` (NOT `the s 190C(4) condition is met`) `add` "s 190C(4): neither certified by every representative body nor shown to be authorised by all the group" `to` (
            EMPTY)))))))))))))

-- s 190A(2): if a s 29 notice (or a s 24MD(6B)(c) notification) is given about an act affecting the area before or while
-- the Registrar considers the claim, "the Registrar must use his or her best endeavours to finish considering the claim by
-- the end of: (e) in a paragraph (a) case--2 months after the notice is given; or (f) in a paragraph (b) case--4 months
-- after the notification day specified in the notice". (2A): "In any other case, the Registrar must finish considering
-- the claim as soon as is practicable." Corresponding State and Territory notices (paras (c), (d)) are not encoded. The
-- date matters because a claimant registered by 4 months after the notification day becomes a native title party
-- (s 30(1)(a)).
DECLARE `Notice about a proposed act` IS ONE OF
    `no such notice`
    `a section 29 notice`
    `a section 24MD(6B)(c) notification`

DECLARE `When should the Registrar finish` IS ONE OF
    `by the end of this day, on best endeavours (s 190A(2))` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `as soon as is practicable; the Act sets no day (s 190A(2A))`

@export By when should the Native Title Registrar finish considering our claim for registration, if a notice about a proposed act (a s 29 right to negotiate notice or a s 24MD(6B)(c) notification) affects our area (Native Title Act 1993 s 190A(2), (2A))?
GIVEN `a section 29 notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a s 29 notice (right to negotiate) about an act affecting any of your claim area was given before or while the Registrar considered the claim
      `the notification day` IS A DATE @desc For a s 29 notice, the notification day it specifies (otherwise any date)
      `a section 24MD notification was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a notification under s 24MD(6B)(c) (compulsory acquisition and similar acts) about an act affecting any of your claim area was given before or while the Registrar considered the claim
      `that notification was given on` IS A DATE @desc For a s 24MD(6B)(c) notification, the day it was given (otherwise any date)
GIVETH A `When should the Registrar finish`
`s 190A(2) -- when should the Registrar finish` `a section 29 notice was given` `the notification day` `a section 24MD notification was given` `that notification was given on` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a section 29 notice was given` AND `a section 24MD notification was given`
        THEN `by the end of this day, on best endeavours (s 190A(2))` (`the earlier of the two`)
        IF `a section 29 notice was given`
        THEN `by the end of this day, on best endeavours (s 190A(2))` (`the notification day` `plus calendar months` 4)
        IF `a section 24MD notification was given`
        THEN `by the end of this day, on best endeavours (s 190A(2))` (`that notification was given on` `plus calendar months` 2)
        OTHERWISE `as soon as is practicable; the Act sets no day (s 190A(2A))`
    WHERE
        `the s 29 day` MEANS `the notification day` `plus calendar months` 4
        `the s 24MD day` MEANS `that notification was given on` `plus calendar months` 2
        `the earlier of the two` MEANS IF `the s 29 day` `is earlier than` `the s 24MD day` THEN `the s 29 day` ELSE `the s 24MD day`

§§ `ss 190D-190F -- If our claim is not registered`

-- s 190E(1): if the Registrar gives the applicant a s 190D(1) notice, "the applicant may apply to the NNTT to reconsider the
-- claim". (2): "The application must: (a) be in writing; and (b) be made within 42 days after the notice under subsection
-- 190D(1) is given; and (c) state the basis on which the reconsideration is sought." (3): not if the applicant has already
-- applied to the Federal Court under s 190F(1). (4): "no more than once". All are the text's no.
-- The 42 days are a regulative rule, counted in days from the day the notice was given (day 0): the last day is that day
-- plus 42 (fork F4).
DECLARE `Claimant party` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant`
    `the person who wants to be a party`
DECLARE `Claimant step` IS ONE OF
    `apply to the NNTT for reconsideration`
    `file the claimant application`
    `notify the Federal Court in writing that I want to be a party`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claimant party` `Claimant step`
`s 190E(2)(b) -- apply for reconsideration within 42 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST `apply to the NNTT for reconsideration`
    WITHIN 42
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "application for reconsideration not made within 42 days after the s 190D(1) notice was given (s 190E(2)(b))"

GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 190E(2)(b) -- applying on this day is in time` `the day` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 190E(2)(b) -- apply for reconsideration within 42 days` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day`), (EVENT `the applicant` `apply to the NNTT for reconsideration` `the day`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export What is the last day on which I (the applicant) can apply to the National Native Title Tribunal to reconsider the Registrar's refusal to register our claim (Native Title Act 1993 s 190E(2)(b))? It is 42 days after the Registrar's notice of the decision was given.
GIVEN `the notice was given on` IS A DATE @desc The day the Registrar gave the applicant notice under s 190D(1) of the decision not to accept the claim
GIVETH A DATE
`s 190E(2)(b) -- the last day to apply for reconsideration` `the notice was given on` MEANS `the notice was given on` `plus days` 42

DECLARE `Can I apply for reconsideration` IS ONE OF
    `yes, in time: apply in writing, stating the basis on which reconsideration is sought (s 190E(1), (2))`
    `no: reconsideration is available only after the Registrar gives notice under s 190D(1) of a decision not to accept the claim (s 190E(1), the text's no)`
    `no: you have already applied to the Federal Court for review under s 190F(1) (s 190E(3), the text's no)`
    `no: you may apply to the NNTT for reconsideration no more than once (s 190E(4), the text's no)`
    `no: out of time, more than 42 days after the notice was given (s 190E(2)(b), the text's no); review by the Federal Court remains (s 190F)`

@export Can I (the applicant) apply to the National Native Title Tribunal to reconsider the Registrar's decision not to register our claim, on the day I plan to apply (Native Title Act 1993 s 190E(1)-(4))?
GIVEN `the Registrar gave notice of refusal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar has given the applicant written notice under s 190D(1) of a decision not to accept the claim for registration
      `the notice was given on` IS A DATE @desc The day that notice was given (otherwise any date)
      `already applied to the Federal Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant has already applied to the Federal Court under s 190F(1) for review of the decision
      `already applied to the NNTT` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant has already applied once to the NNTT to reconsider this claim
      `applying on` IS A DATE @desc The day the application for reconsideration is (or will be) made
GIVETH A `Can I apply for reconsideration`
`s 190E -- can I apply for reconsideration` `the Registrar gave notice of refusal` `the notice was given on` `already applied to the Federal Court` `already applied to the NNTT` `applying on` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the Registrar gave notice of refusal`)
        THEN `no: reconsideration is available only after the Registrar gives notice under s 190D(1) of a decision not to accept the claim (s 190E(1), the text's no)`
        IF `already applied to the Federal Court`
        THEN `no: you have already applied to the Federal Court for review under s 190F(1) (s 190E(3), the text's no)`
        IF `already applied to the NNTT`
        THEN `no: you may apply to the NNTT for reconsideration no more than once (s 190E(4), the text's no)`
        IF `s 190E(2)(b) -- applying on this day is in time` (`the day number of` `applying on` `counted from` `the notice was given on`)
        THEN `yes, in time: apply in writing, stating the basis on which reconsideration is sought (s 190E(1), (2))`
        OTHERWISE `no: out of time, more than 42 days after the notice was given (s 190E(2)(b), the text's no); review by the Federal Court remains (s 190F)`

-- s 190F(1): after a s 190D(1) notice "the applicant may apply to the Federal Court for a review of the Registrar's
-- decision not to accept the claim, provided the NNTT is not reconsidering the claim under section 190E at the time the
-- application is made". The Act sets no time limit (any limit is in the Federal Court's rules, not deposited).
-- s 190F(3): where the only reason for refusal was s 190B(7) (s 190D(2)), "the Court may order the Registrar to accept the
-- claim" if satisfied that (a) prima facie some rights can be established and (b) at some time in his or her lifetime at
-- least one parent of one member had a traditional physical connection and would reasonably have been expected to have
-- maintained it but for things done by the Crown, a statutory authority or a leaseholder.
-- s 190F(6): once every avenue of review is exhausted without registration, the Court may dismiss the application if
-- satisfied it has not been and is not likely to be amended to a different outcome, and there is no other reason not to.
DECLARE `Can I seek review by the Federal Court` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you may apply for review; as the only reason for refusal was physical connection, the Court may order the Registrar to accept the claim, since it is satisfied of s 190F(3)(a) and (b)`
    `yes: you may apply for review of the Registrar's decision (s 190F(1)); the Act sets no time limit`
    `no: review is available only after the Registrar gives notice under s 190D(1) of a decision not to accept the claim (s 190F(1), the text's no)`
    `not now: you cannot apply while the NNTT is reconsidering the claim under s 190E (s 190F(1), the text's no)`

@export Can I (the applicant) apply to the Federal Court for review of the Registrar's decision not to register our claim, and can the Court order registration where the claim failed only the physical connection test (Native Title Act 1993 s 190F(1), (3))?
GIVEN `the Registrar gave notice of refusal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar has given the applicant written notice under s 190D(1) of a decision not to accept the claim
      `the NNTT is reconsidering the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the NNTT is reconsidering the claim under s 190E at the time you apply to the Court
      `the only failure was physical connection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only reason the claim was not accepted was the physical connection condition in s 190B(7)
      `the Court is satisfied of a parent's connection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court is satisfied that prima facie some rights can be established, and that at least one parent of one member had a traditional physical connection that would have been maintained but for things done by the Crown, a statutory authority or a leaseholder (s 190F(3))
GIVETH A `Can I seek review by the Federal Court`
`s 190F -- can I seek review by the Federal Court` `the Registrar gave notice of refusal` `the NNTT is reconsidering the claim` `the only failure was physical connection` `the Court is satisfied of a parent's connection` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the Registrar gave notice of refusal`)
        THEN `no: review is available only after the Registrar gives notice under s 190D(1) of a decision not to accept the claim (s 190F(1), the text's no)`
        IF `the NNTT is reconsidering the claim`
        THEN `not now: you cannot apply while the NNTT is reconsidering the claim under s 190E (s 190F(1), the text's no)`
        IF `the only failure was physical connection` AND `the Court is satisfied of a parent's connection`
        THEN `yes: you may apply for review; as the only reason for refusal was physical connection, the Court may order the Registrar to accept the claim, since it is satisfied of s 190F(3)(a) and (b)`
        OTHERWISE `yes: you may apply for review of the Registrar's decision (s 190F(1)); the Act sets no time limit`

§§ `ss 66, 84 -- Am I a party to the proceedings on an application over our area?`

-- s 66(10)(c): the notice of an application must state that "a person who wants to be a party in relation to the
-- application must notify the Federal Court, in writing, within the period of 3 months starting on the notification day
-- ..., or, after that period, get the leave of the Federal Court under subsection 84(5) to become a party".
-- s 84(2): the applicant is a party. s 84(3): another person is a party "if: (a) ... (i) the person is covered by any of
-- subparagraphs 66(3)(a)(i) to (vi) [among them a registered native title claimant or registered native title body
-- corporate for any of the area]; (ii) the person claims to hold native title in relation to land or waters in the area
-- covered by the application; (iii) the person's interest ... may be affected by a determination in the proceedings; and
-- (b) the person notifies the Federal Court, in writing, that the person wants to be a party ... (i) within the period
-- specified in the notice under section 66". s 84(5): "The Federal Court may at any time join any person as a party ...
-- if the Court is satisfied that the person's interests may be affected ... and it is in the interests of justice".
-- The period "of 3 months starting on the notification day" includes that day: the last day is the day before the same
-- day 3 months on, or the last day of that month if it has no such day (forks F1, F5). Counted in days from the
-- notification day (day 0). The duty is on the person who wants to be a party, not the applicant, who is a party
-- already (s 84(2)).
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claimant party` `Claimant step`
`s 66(10)(c) -- notify the Federal Court within 3 months` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the person who wants to be a party`
    MUST `notify the Federal Court in writing that I want to be a party`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person who wants to be a party` BECAUSE "notice not given within the period of 3 months starting on the notification day: leave of the Federal Court is needed to become a party (ss 66(10)(c), 84(3)(b), 84(5))"

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 66(10)(c) -- notifying on this day is in time` `the days allowed` `the day` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 66(10)(c) -- notify the Federal Court within 3 months` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day`), (EVENT `the person who wants to be a party` `notify the Federal Court in writing that I want to be a party` `the day`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export What is the last day on which I can notify the Federal Court in writing that I want to be a party to a native title or compensation application over land I claim, without needing the Court's leave (Native Title Act 1993 ss 66(10)(c), 84(3)(b))? The period is 3 months starting on the notification day in the notice of the application.
GIVEN `the notification day` IS A DATE @desc The notification day specified in the Registrar's notice of the application
GIVETH A DATE
`s 66(10)(c) -- the last day to notify the Federal Court` `the notification day` MEANS `the last day of` 3 `months starting on` `the notification day`

DECLARE `Am I a party` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the applicant is a party (s 84(2))`
    `yes: you notified the Federal Court in time, and you are a person s 84(3)(a) covers (s 84(3))`
    `yes: the Federal Court has joined you as a party (s 84(5))`
    `not yet: notify the Federal Court in writing by the last day` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `no: the period of 3 months starting on the notification day has ended (ss 66(10)(c), 84(3)(b), the text's no); the Court may still join you if satisfied your interests may be affected and it is in the interests of justice (s 84(5))`
    `not under s 84(3): you are not a person it covers (the text's no); the Court may still join you if satisfied your interests may be affected and it is in the interests of justice (s 84(5))`

@export Am I a party to the Federal Court proceedings on a native title or compensation application over land or waters I claim, and if not yet, by when must I notify the Court (Native Title Act 1993 ss 66(10)(c), 84(2), (3), (5))?
GIVEN `I am the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are (or are one of the persons who are) the applicant for this application
      `I claim native title in the area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you claim to hold native title in land or waters in the area the application covers
      `I am a registered claimant or body corporate for the area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a registered native title claimant or registered native title body corporate for any of the area (or otherwise a person listed in s 66(3)(a)(i)-(vi))
      `my interest may be affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your interest in land or waters may be affected by a determination in the proceedings
      `the notification day` IS A DATE @desc The notification day specified in the notice of the application
      `I have notified the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have notified the Federal Court in writing that you want to be a party
      `notified on` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day you notified it (otherwise any date)
      `the Court has joined me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Federal Court has ordered that you be joined as a party under s 84(5)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH AN `Am I a party`
`ss 66, 84 -- am I a party` `I am the applicant` `I claim native title in the area` `I am a registered claimant or body corporate for the area` `my interest may be affected` `the notification day` `I have notified the Court` `notified on` `the Court has joined me` `today` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `I am the applicant`
        THEN `yes: the applicant is a party (s 84(2))`
        IF `the Court has joined me`
        THEN `yes: the Federal Court has joined you as a party (s 84(5))`
        IF (NOT `covered by s 84(3)(a)`)
        THEN `not under s 84(3): you are not a person it covers (the text's no); the Court may still join you if satisfied your interests may be affected and it is in the interests of justice (s 84(5))`
        IF `I have notified the Court` AND `s 66(10)(c) -- notifying on this day is in time` `the days allowed` (`the day number of` `notified on` `counted from` `the notification day`)
        THEN `yes: you notified the Federal Court in time, and you are a person s 84(3)(a) covers (s 84(3))`
        IF (NOT `I have notified the Court`) AND `today` `is on or before` `the last day`
        THEN `not yet: notify the Federal Court in writing by the last day` `the last day`
        OTHERWISE `no: the period of 3 months starting on the notification day has ended (ss 66(10)(c), 84(3)(b), the text's no); the Court may still join you if satisfied your interests may be affected and it is in the interests of justice (s 84(5))`
    WHERE
        `covered by s 84(3)(a)` MEANS `I claim native title in the area` OR `I am a registered claimant or body corporate for the area` OR `my interest may be affected`
        `the last day` MEANS `s 66(10)(c) -- the last day to notify the Federal Court` `the notification day`
        `the days allowed` MEANS `the day number of` `the last day` `counted from` `the notification day`

§§ `s 66B -- Can I apply to replace our applicant?`

-- s 66B(1): one or more members of the claim group may apply to the Federal Court for an order that they replace the
-- current applicant "on the grounds that: (a) one or more of the following applies to a person who is ... the current
-- applicant: (i) the person consents to his or her replacement or removal; (iii) the person is no longer authorised by
-- the claim group ...; (iv) the person has exceeded the authority given to him or her by the claim group ...; and (b) the
-- member or members are authorised by the claim group to make the application and to deal with matters arising".
-- (2): "The Court may make the order if it is satisfied that the grounds are established."
-- s 66B(2A): if a person who is (alone or jointly) the current applicant dies or is unable to act because of physical or
-- mental incapacity, one or more members may apply for an order under (2B), which lets the Court order replacement by a
-- newly authorised member with continuing members, by the continuing members, or by the applying members if authorised.
-- The grounds are read as a closed list ("on the grounds that"): fork F6.
DECLARE `Can I apply to replace the applicant` IS ONE OF
    `yes, under s 66B(2A): a member of the group may apply because a person who is the applicant has died or cannot act; the Court may order replacement as s 66B(2B) allows`
    `yes, under s 66B(1): you may apply to replace the applicant; the Court may order it if satisfied the grounds are established (s 66B(2))`
    `no: only a member of the claim group may apply (s 66B(1), (2A), the text's no)`
    `no: none of the s 66B(1)(a) grounds applies to the current applicant (consent, no longer authorised, exceeded authority), and no one has died or become incapable (the text's no)`
    `no: you (the members applying) must be authorised by the claim group to make the application and deal with matters arising (s 66B(1)(b), the text's no)`

@export Can I (with other members of our claim group) apply to the Federal Court to replace the person who is our group's applicant (Native Title Act 1993 s 66B)?
GIVEN `I am a member of the claim group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member of the native title claim group (or compensation claim group) for the application
      `the applicant consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person who is (alone or jointly) the current applicant consents to being replaced or removed
      `the applicant is no longer authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person who is the current applicant is no longer authorised by the claim group to make the application and deal with matters arising
      `the applicant exceeded authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person who is the current applicant has exceeded the authority the claim group gave
      `the applicant died or cannot act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person who is the current applicant has died or cannot act because of physical or mental incapacity
      `we are authorised by the group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (the members applying) are authorised by the claim group to make the application and deal with matters arising
GIVETH A `Can I apply to replace the applicant`
`s 66B -- can I apply to replace the applicant` `I am a member of the claim group` `the applicant consents` `the applicant is no longer authorised` `the applicant exceeded authority` `the applicant died or cannot act` `we are authorised by the group` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `I am a member of the claim group`)
        THEN `no: only a member of the claim group may apply (s 66B(1), (2A), the text's no)`
        IF `the applicant died or cannot act`
        THEN `yes, under s 66B(2A): a member of the group may apply because a person who is the applicant has died or cannot act; the Court may order replacement as s 66B(2B) allows`
        IF (NOT (`the applicant consents` OR `the applicant is no longer authorised` OR `the applicant exceeded authority`))
        THEN `no: none of the s 66B(1)(a) grounds applies to the current applicant (consent, no longer authorised, exceeded authority), and no one has died or become incapable (the text's no)`
        IF `we are authorised by the group`
        THEN `yes, under s 66B(1): you may apply to replace the applicant; the Court may order it if satisfied the grounds are established (s 66B(2))`
        OTHERWISE `no: you (the members applying) must be authorised by the claim group to make the application and deal with matters arising (s 66B(1)(b), the text's no)`

§§ `ss 29, 30 -- Are we a native title party for a proposed act (the right to negotiate)?`

-- s 29(2)(b)(i): the Government party must give notice to "any registered native title claimant (also a native title
-- party)" in relation to the affected land or waters, "unless there are one or more registered native title bodies
-- corporate in relation to all of the land or waters that will be affected".
-- s 30(1)(a): also a native title party is "any applicant who, 4 months after the notification day ..., is a registered
-- native title claimant in relation to any of the land or waters that will be affected by the act, so long as: (i) the
-- application containing the claim was filed in the Federal Court, or given to the recognised State/Territory body,
-- before the end of 3 months after the notification day; and (ii) the claim related to any of the land or waters that will be affected".
-- s 30(2): "A registered native title claimant ceases to be a native title party if the registered native title claimant
-- ceases to be a registered native title claimant."
-- s 30(1)(a)(i) as a regulative rule: file the application within the days from the notification day (day 0) to the day
-- 3 months after it (fork F5: "before the end of 3 months after" a day includes the day 3 months on). Being registered
-- "4 months after the notification day" is read as: the claim was entered on the Register on or before that day and has
-- stayed on it. Filing in the Federal Court and giving the application to a recognised State/Territory body are one
-- input: the day the application was filed or given, whichever came first.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Claimant party` `Claimant step`
`s 30(1)(a)(i) -- file the claimant application within 3 months` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST `file the claimant application`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "claimant application not filed before the end of 3 months after the notification day: the applicant cannot become a native title party under s 30(1)(a)"

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 30(1)(a)(i) -- filing on this day is in time` `the days allowed` `the day` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 30(1)(a)(i) -- file the claimant application within 3 months` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day`), (EVENT `the applicant` `file the claimant application` `the day`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export What is the last day to file our claimant application, and the day by which the claim must be on the Register of Native Title Claims, for us to become a native title party with the right to negotiate about a proposed act (Native Title Act 1993 s 30(1)(a))? Returns the two days: the last day to file (3 months after the notification day) and the registration day (4 months after).
GIVEN `the notification day` IS A DATE @desc The notification day specified in the s 29 notice of the proposed act
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`s 30(1)(a) -- the last day to file and the day to be registered by` `the notification day` MEANS
    LIST (`the notification day` `plus calendar months` 3), (`the notification day` `plus calendar months` 4)

DECLARE `Are we a native title party` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you were a registered native title claimant for the affected area when notice was given, so you are a native title party (s 29(2)(b)(i))`
    `yes: the application was filed in time and the claim was on the Register 4 months after the notification day (s 30(1)(a))`
    `not yet: the application was filed in time; you will be a native title party if the claim is on the Register by this day` HAS `the registration day` IS A DATE
    `no: the claim does not relate to any of the land or waters the act will affect (ss 29(2), 30(1)(a)(ii), the text's no)`
    `no: you have ceased to be a registered native title claimant, so you have ceased to be a native title party (s 30(2), the text's no)`
    `no: the application was not filed before the end of 3 months after the notification day (s 30(1)(a)(i), the text's no)`
    `no: the claim was not on the Register 4 months after the notification day (s 30(1)(a), the text's no)`

@export Are we (our group's applicant) a native title party for an act the government proposes to do over our claim area, with the right to negotiate about it (Native Title Act 1993 ss 29(2)(b), 30(1)(a), 30(2))?
GIVEN `the claim relates to the affected area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim relates to any of the land or waters the proposed act will affect
      `the notification day` IS A DATE @desc The notification day specified in the s 29 notice
      `registered when notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim was already on the Register of Native Title Claims when the s 29 notice was given
      `a body corporate covers all the affected area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there are registered native title bodies corporate for all of the land or waters the act will affect
      `the application was filed on` IS A DATE @desc The day your claimant application was filed in the Federal Court, or given to the recognised State/Territory body (s 30(1)(a)(i)), whichever was first
      `the claim has been entered on the Register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim has been entered on the Register of Native Title Claims
      `entered on` IS A DATE @desc If entered, the day it was entered (otherwise any date)
      `the claim is still on the Register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If entered, whether it is still on the Register (it has not been removed); answer yes if it has never been entered
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH AN `Are we a native title party`
`ss 29, 30 -- are we a native title party` `the claim relates to the affected area` `the notification day` `registered when notice was given` `a body corporate covers all the affected area` `the application was filed on` `the claim has been entered on the Register` `entered on` `the claim is still on the Register` `today` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the claim relates to the affected area`)
        THEN `no: the claim does not relate to any of the land or waters the act will affect (ss 29(2), 30(1)(a)(ii), the text's no)`
        IF `the claim has been entered on the Register` AND (NOT `the claim is still on the Register`)
        THEN `no: you have ceased to be a registered native title claimant, so you have ceased to be a native title party (s 30(2), the text's no)`
        IF `registered when notice was given` AND (NOT `a body corporate covers all the affected area`)
        THEN `yes: you were a registered native title claimant for the affected area when notice was given, so you are a native title party (s 29(2)(b)(i))`
        IF (NOT (`s 30(1)(a)(i) -- filing on this day is in time` `the days to file` (`the day number of` `the application was filed on` `counted from` `the notification day`)))
        THEN `no: the application was not filed before the end of 3 months after the notification day (s 30(1)(a)(i), the text's no)`
        IF `the claim has been entered on the Register` AND `entered on` `is on or before` `the registration day`
        THEN `yes: the application was filed in time and the claim was on the Register 4 months after the notification day (s 30(1)(a))`
        IF (NOT `the claim has been entered on the Register`) AND `today` `is on or before` `the registration day`
        THEN `not yet: the application was filed in time; you will be a native title party if the claim is on the Register by this day` `the registration day`
        OTHERWISE `no: the claim was not on the Register 4 months after the notification day (s 30(1)(a), the text's no)`
    WHERE
        `the registration day` MEANS `the notification day` `plus calendar months` 4
        `the days to file` MEANS `the day number of` (`the notification day` `plus calendar months` 3) `counted from` `the notification day`

§§ `s 32 -- The expedited procedure: can the act go ahead without negotiating with us?`

-- s 32(2): "If the native title parties do not lodge an objection with the arbitral body in accordance with subsection
-- (3), the Government party may do the act." (3): "A native title party may, within the period of 4 months after the
-- notification day ..., lodge an objection with the arbitral body against the inclusion of the statement." (4): on an
-- objection, the arbitral body determines whether the act attracts the expedited procedure; if it does, the Government
-- party may do the act. (5): if not, s 31(1) applies (negotiation). (6): if all objections are withdrawn, the
-- Government party may do the act. (7): if the Government party withdraws the statement, s 31(1) applies.
-- "Within the period of 4 months after the notification day": the last day is the day 4 months on (fork F5).
@export What is the last day for us, as a native title party, to lodge an objection with the arbitral body to the government's statement that a proposed act attracts the expedited procedure (Native Title Act 1993 s 32(3))? It is 4 months after the notification day.
GIVEN `the notification day` IS A DATE @desc The notification day specified in the s 29 notice
GIVETH A DATE
`s 32(3) -- the last day to object` `the notification day` MEANS `the notification day` `plus calendar months` 4

DECLARE `Arbitral body finding on the expedited procedure` IS ONE OF
    `not yet determined`
    `the act attracts the expedited procedure`
    `the act does not attract the expedited procedure`

DECLARE `Can the act go ahead without negotiating with us` IS ONE OF
    `no: the notice did not say the act attracts the expedited procedure, so the negotiation parties must negotiate in good faith (s 31(1))`
    `no: the Government party withdrew its expedited procedure statement, so the negotiation parties must negotiate in good faith (ss 32(7), 31(1))`
    `no: the arbitral body determined the act does not attract the expedited procedure, so the negotiation parties must negotiate in good faith (ss 32(5), 31(1))`
    `not yet: your objection is lodged and the arbitral body has not yet determined it (s 32(4))`
    `not yet: you may still object, until the last day` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `yes: no objection was lodged within 4 months after the notification day, so the Government party may do the act (s 32(2))`
    `yes: every objection was withdrawn, so the Government party may do the act (s 32(6))`
    `yes: the arbitral body determined the act attracts the expedited procedure, so the Government party may do the act (s 32(4))`

@export Can the government do a proposed act over our area without negotiating with us, under the expedited procedure (Native Title Act 1993 ss 31(1), 32)?
GIVEN `the notice says expedited procedure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the s 29 notice includes a statement that the Government party considers the act attracts the expedited procedure
      `the government withdrew the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Government party has given written notice withdrawing that statement
      `the notification day` IS A DATE @desc The notification day specified in the s 29 notice
      `an objection was lodged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a native title party lodged an objection with the arbitral body against the statement
      `lodged on` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it was lodged (otherwise any date)
      `all objections were withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every objection lodged has since been withdrawn
      `the arbitral body found the act attracts it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the arbitral body has determined that the act attracts the expedited procedure
      `the arbitral body found the act does not attract it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the arbitral body has determined that the act does not attract the expedited procedure
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Can the act go ahead without negotiating with us`
`s 32 -- can the act go ahead without negotiating with us` `the notice says expedited procedure` `the government withdrew the statement` `the notification day` `an objection was lodged` `lodged on` `all objections were withdrawn` `the arbitral body found the act attracts it` `the arbitral body found the act does not attract it` `today` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the notice says expedited procedure`)
        THEN `no: the notice did not say the act attracts the expedited procedure, so the negotiation parties must negotiate in good faith (s 31(1))`
        IF `the government withdrew the statement`
        THEN `no: the Government party withdrew its expedited procedure statement, so the negotiation parties must negotiate in good faith (ss 32(7), 31(1))`
        IF `an objection in time`
        THEN `the answer on a timely objection`
        IF `today` `is on or before` `the last day`
        THEN `not yet: you may still object, until the last day` `the last day`
        OTHERWISE `yes: no objection was lodged within 4 months after the notification day, so the Government party may do the act (s 32(2))`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `s 32(3) -- the last day to object` `the notification day`
        `an objection in time` MEANS `an objection was lodged` AND `lodged on` `is on or before` `the last day`
        `the answer on a timely objection` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the arbitral body found the act does not attract it`
                THEN `no: the arbitral body determined the act does not attract the expedited procedure, so the negotiation parties must negotiate in good faith (ss 32(5), 31(1))`
                IF `the arbitral body found the act attracts it`
                THEN `yes: the arbitral body determined the act attracts the expedited procedure, so the Government party may do the act (s 32(4))`
                IF `all objections were withdrawn`
                THEN `yes: every objection was withdrawn, so the Government party may do the act (s 32(6))`
                OTHERWISE `not yet: your objection is lodged and the arbitral body has not yet determined it (s 32(4))`

§§ `ss 31(1C), 35-38 -- Negotiation, agreement and the arbitral body`

-- s 31(1C): "The requirement that a native title party that is a registered native title claimant be a party to the
-- agreement is satisfied if: (a) a majority of the persons who comprise the registered native title claimant are parties
-- to the agreement, unless paragraph (b) applies; or (b) if conditions under section 251BA on the authority of the
-- registered native title claimant provide for the persons who must become a party to the agreement--those persons are
-- parties to the agreement." "Majority" is read as more than half. (1D): the majority must notify the others within a
-- reasonable period; failure does not invalidate the agreement.
DECLARE `Is our registered claimant a party to the agreement` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the persons the s 251BA conditions name are all parties to the agreement (s 31(1C)(b))`
    `yes: a majority of the persons who comprise the registered native title claimant are parties (s 31(1C)(a)); they must tell the others within a reasonable period (s 31(1D))`
    `no: the s 251BA conditions name who must be parties, and not all of them are (s 31(1C)(b), the text's no)`
    `no: fewer than a majority of the persons who comprise the registered native title claimant are parties (s 31(1C)(a), the text's no)`

@export Is our registered native title claimant (the persons who are jointly our group's applicant) a party to a right to negotiate agreement, given how many of those persons have signed it (Native Title Act 1993 s 31(1C), (1D))?
GIVEN `the number of persons who comprise our applicant` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons are jointly the registered native title claimant (your group's applicant)
      `the number who are parties` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them are parties to the agreement
      `conditions name who must be parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether conditions under s 251BA on the applicant's authority say which persons must become parties to such an agreement
      `those persons are all parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, whether all of those persons are parties to the agreement
GIVETH AN `Is our registered claimant a party to the agreement`
`s 31(1C) -- is our registered claimant a party to the agreement` `the number of persons who comprise our applicant` `the number who are parties` `conditions name who must be parties` `those persons are all parties` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `conditions name who must be parties` AND `those persons are all parties`
        THEN `yes: the persons the s 251BA conditions name are all parties to the agreement (s 31(1C)(b))`
        IF `conditions name who must be parties`
        THEN `no: the s 251BA conditions name who must be parties, and not all of them are (s 31(1C)(b), the text's no)`
        IF (`the number who are parties` TIMES 2) GREATER THAN `the number of persons who comprise our applicant`
        THEN `yes: a majority of the persons who comprise the registered native title claimant are parties (s 31(1C)(a)); they must tell the others within a reasonable period (s 31(1D))`
        OTHERWISE `no: fewer than a majority of the persons who comprise the registered native title claimant are parties (s 31(1C)(a), the text's no)`

-- s 35(1): "Any negotiation party may apply to the arbitral body for a determination under section 38 in relation to the
-- act if: (a) at least 6 months have passed since the notification day ...; and (b) no agreement of the kind mentioned in
-- paragraph 31(1)(b) has been made". 6 months "have passed since" the notification day at the end of the day 6 months
-- on, so the first day to apply is the day after it (fork F7).
@export What is the first day on which we, as a negotiation party, can apply to the arbitral body for a determination whether a proposed act may be done, if no agreement has been reached (Native Title Act 1993 s 35(1))?
GIVEN `the notification day` IS A DATE @desc The notification day specified in the s 29 notice
GIVETH A DATE
`s 35(1) -- the first day to apply for a determination` `the notification day` MEANS (`the notification day` `plus calendar months` 6) `plus days` 1

DECLARE `Can we apply for an arbitral body determination` IS ONE OF
    `yes: at least 6 months have passed since the notification day and no agreement has been made (s 35(1)); you may withdraw the application, and keep negotiating, until a determination is made (s 35(2), (3))`
    `no: an agreement has been made about the act (s 35(1)(b), the text's no)`
    `not yet: 6 months have not passed since the notification day (s 35(1)(a), the text's no); the first day is` HAS `the first day` IS A DATE

@export Can we, as a native title party, apply to the arbitral body for a determination whether a proposed act may be done, on the day we plan to apply (Native Title Act 1993 s 35)?
GIVEN `the notification day` IS A DATE @desc The notification day specified in the s 29 notice
      `an agreement has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an agreement under s 31(1)(b) about the act has been made
      `applying on` IS A DATE @desc The day you plan to apply
GIVETH A `Can we apply for an arbitral body determination`
`s 35 -- can we apply for an arbitral body determination` `the notification day` `an agreement has been made` `applying on` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an agreement has been made`
        THEN `no: an agreement has been made about the act (s 35(1)(b), the text's no)`
        IF `applying on` `is earlier than` `the first day`
        THEN `not yet: 6 months have not passed since the notification day (s 35(1)(a), the text's no); the first day is` `the first day`
        OTHERWISE `yes: at least 6 months have passed since the notification day and no agreement has been made (s 35(1)); you may withdraw the application, and keep negotiating, until a determination is made (s 35(2), (3))`
    WHERE
        `the first day` MEANS `s 35(1) -- the first day to apply for a determination` `the notification day`

-- s 37: "The arbitral body must not make a determination if: (a) an agreement of the kind mentioned in paragraph 31(1)(b)
-- has been made; or (b) a determination under section 36A has been made."
-- s 36(2): "If any negotiation party satisfies the arbitral body that any other negotiation party (other than a native
-- title party) did not negotiate in good faith ..., the arbitral body must not make the determination on the
-- application." (the note: a further application may be made under s 35).
-- s 38(1): "Except where section 37 applies, the arbitral body must make one of the following determinations: (a) ... the
-- act must not be done; (b) ... the act may be done; (c) ... the act may be done subject to conditions". Which one is for
-- the arbitral body, on the s 39 criteria (an input it decides; not encoded).
-- s 38(2): "The arbitral body must not determine a condition under paragraph (1)(c) that has the effect that native title
-- parties are to be entitled to payments worked out by reference to: (a) the amount of profits made; or (b) any income
-- derived; or (c) any things produced" by a grantee party. s 33(1): an agreement may include such a condition.
DECLARE `What the arbitral body must do on our application` IS ONE OF
    `it must make one of three determinations: the act must not be done, may be done, or may be done subject to conditions (s 38(1)); a condition cannot give you a share of profits, income or production (s 38(2)), though an agreement can (s 33(1))`
    `nothing: the application has been withdrawn (s 35(2), (3))`
    `it must not make a determination: an agreement has been made (s 37(a), the text's no)`
    `it must not make a determination: the Minister has made a s 36A determination (s 37(b), the text's no)`
    `it must not make the determination: another negotiation party did not negotiate in good faith (s 36(2), the text's no); a further application may be made under s 35`

@export What must the arbitral body do on an application for a determination whether a proposed act over our area may be done, and can it give us a share of the profits (Native Title Act 1993 ss 33(1), 35(3), 36(2), 37, 38)?
GIVEN `the application was withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application has been withdrawn, or an agreement made before a determination (which counts as withdrawal)
      `an agreement has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an agreement under s 31(1)(b) has been made about the act
      `the Minister made a determination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the relevant Minister has made a determination under s 36A about the act
      `another party did not negotiate in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a negotiation party has satisfied the arbitral body that another negotiation party (the government or the grantee, not a native title party) did not negotiate in good faith
GIVETH A `What the arbitral body must do on our application`
`ss 36-38 -- what the arbitral body must do on our application` `the application was withdrawn` `an agreement has been made` `the Minister made a determination` `another party did not negotiate in good faith` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the application was withdrawn`
        THEN `nothing: the application has been withdrawn (s 35(2), (3))`
        IF `an agreement has been made`
        THEN `it must not make a determination: an agreement has been made (s 37(a), the text's no)`
        IF `the Minister made a determination`
        THEN `it must not make a determination: the Minister has made a s 36A determination (s 37(b), the text's no)`
        IF `another party did not negotiate in good faith`
        THEN `it must not make the determination: another negotiation party did not negotiate in good faith (s 36(2), the text's no); a further application may be made under s 35`
        OTHERWISE `it must make one of three determinations: the act must not be done, may be done, or may be done subject to conditions (s 38(1)); a condition cannot give you a share of profits, income or production (s 38(2)), though an agreement can (s 33(1))`

-- s 41(1): a determination, or a s 31(1)(b) agreement, "that the act may be done subject to conditions being complied with
-- by the parties has effect, if the act is done, as if the conditions were terms of a contract among the negotiation
-- parties". (2): "If a native title party is a registered native title claimant, any other person included in the native
-- title claim group concerned is taken to be a negotiation party for the purposes only of subsection (1)."
DECLARE `Can I enforce the conditions as contract terms` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the conditions have effect as terms of a contract among the negotiation parties, and you are one (s 41(1))`
    `yes: as a member of the claim group of a registered native title claimant that is a native title party, you are taken to be a negotiation party for this purpose (s 41(2)), so the conditions bind as contract terms (s 41(1))`
    `not yet: the conditions take effect as contract terms only if the act is done (s 41(1), the text's no)`
    `no: s 41(1) applies only to a determination or agreement that the act may be done subject to conditions (the text's no)`
    `not under s 41: you are neither a negotiation party nor a member of the claim group of a registered native title claimant that is a native title party (NOTHING-kind)`

@export Can I enforce the conditions in a right to negotiate agreement or arbitral determination as if they were contract terms (Native Title Act 1993 s 41(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the act may be done subject to conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the arbitral body's determination, or the s 31(1)(b) agreement, is that the act may be done subject to conditions
      `the act has been done` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act (for example the grant of the mining lease) has been done
      `I am a negotiation party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are yourself a negotiation party (the government party, a native title party or a grantee party)
      `I am in the claim group of a registered claimant party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member of the native title claim group of a registered native title claimant that is a native title party for the act
GIVETH A `Can I enforce the conditions as contract terms`
`s 41 -- can I enforce the conditions as contract terms` `the act may be done subject to conditions` `the act has been done` `I am a negotiation party` `I am in the claim group of a registered claimant party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the act may be done subject to conditions`)
        THEN `no: s 41(1) applies only to a determination or agreement that the act may be done subject to conditions (the text's no)`
        IF (NOT `the act has been done`)
        THEN `not yet: the conditions take effect as contract terms only if the act is done (s 41(1), the text's no)`
        IF `I am a negotiation party`
        THEN `yes: the conditions have effect as terms of a contract among the negotiation parties, and you are one (s 41(1))`
        IF `I am in the claim group of a registered claimant party`
        THEN `yes: as a member of the claim group of a registered native title claimant that is a native title party, you are taken to be a negotiation party for this purpose (s 41(2)), so the conditions bind as contract terms (s 41(1))`
        OTHERWISE `not under s 41: you are neither a negotiation party nor a member of the claim group of a registered native title claimant that is a native title party (NOTHING-kind)`

§§ `s 61 -- Can we make a compensation application?`

-- s 61(1), table, "Compensation application" (an application under s 50(2)), persons who may make it: "(1) A registered
-- native title body corporate, if the determination is sought in relation to an area ... in relation to which the
-- registered native title body corporate holds, or is an agent prescribed body corporate in relation to, the native
-- title rights and interests; or (1A) A registered native title body corporate, on behalf of all the persons who claim to
-- be entitled to the compensation, if: (a) the ... area (the extinguished area) ... is within the external boundary of
-- the area ... covered by an approved determination ... under which the registered native title body corporate holds ...
-- native title rights and interests; and (b) either: (i) the earlier determination is that native title does not exist
-- in relation to the extinguished area; or (ii) the extinguished area was expressly excluded ... because of subsection
-- 61A(2); and (c) the persons who claim to be entitled to the compensation are the common law holders in relation to the
-- earlier determination; or (2) A person or persons authorised by all the persons (the compensation claim group) who
-- claim to be entitled to the compensation, provided the person or persons are also included in the compensation claim
-- group." As for claimant applications, the table is read as closed (fork F3).
DECLARE `Can we make a compensation application` IS ONE OF
    `yes: our registered native title body corporate may apply, as it holds (or is agent for) the native title in the area (s 61(1), compensation item 1)`
    `yes: our registered native title body corporate may apply on behalf of all who claim the compensation, for the extinguished area inside its determination (s 61(1), compensation item 1A)`
    `yes: the person or persons our compensation claim group authorised may apply, and will jointly be the applicant (s 61(1), compensation item 2, s 61(2))`
    `no: none of the persons s 61(1) lists for a compensation application is applying on these facts (the text's no)`

@export Can our group (through a person we authorise) or our registered native title body corporate apply to the Federal Court for a determination of compensation for acts affecting our native title (Native Title Act 1993 ss 50(2), 61(1), 251B)?
GIVEN `our body corporate holds the native title in the area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a registered native title body corporate holds (or is an agent prescribed body corporate for) the native title rights and interests in the area the compensation is sought for
      `the area is an extinguished area inside our determination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the area lies within the external boundary of an approved determination under which your body corporate holds native title, and that determination found no native title there or excluded the area because of s 61A(2)
      `we are the common law holders under that determination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the persons claiming the compensation are the common law holders under that earlier determination
      `the applicant is in the compensation claim group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person (or each of the persons) who will apply is a member of the group of persons who claim to be entitled to the compensation
      `a traditional process must be followed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, under your group's traditional laws and customs, there is a process of decision-making that must be followed to authorise things of this kind
      `authorised by the traditional process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is such a process, whether the group authorised the applicant in accordance with it
      `authorised by an agreed and adopted process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is no such process, whether the group authorised the applicant under a decision-making process it agreed to and adopted
GIVETH A `Can we make a compensation application`
`s 61 -- can we make a compensation application` `our body corporate holds the native title in the area` `the area is an extinguished area inside our determination` `we are the common law holders under that determination` `the applicant is in the compensation claim group` `a traditional process must be followed` `authorised by the traditional process` `authorised by an agreed and adopted process` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `our body corporate holds the native title in the area`
        THEN `yes: our registered native title body corporate may apply, as it holds (or is agent for) the native title in the area (s 61(1), compensation item 1)`
        IF `the area is an extinguished area inside our determination` AND `we are the common law holders under that determination`
        THEN `yes: our registered native title body corporate may apply on behalf of all who claim the compensation, for the extinguished area inside its determination (s 61(1), compensation item 1A)`
        IF `the applicant is in the compensation claim group` AND `s 251B -- the applicant is authorised by all the persons in the group` `a traditional process must be followed` `authorised by the traditional process` `authorised by an agreed and adopted process`
        THEN `yes: the person or persons our compensation claim group authorised may apply, and will jointly be the applicant (s 61(1), compensation item 2, s 61(2))`
        OTHERWISE `no: none of the persons s 61(1) lists for a compensation application is applying on these facts (the text's no)`

§§ `ss 49-51A, 53 -- What compensation can we get?`

-- s 51(1): "the entitlement to compensation ... is an entitlement on just terms to compensate the native title holders for
-- any loss, diminution, impairment or other effect of the act on their native title rights and interests".
-- (2): for a compulsory acquisition, the court "may ... have regard to" the principles in the acquisition law.
-- (3): if the act is not a compulsory acquisition and the similar compensable interest test (s 240) is satisfied, the
-- court "must ... apply" the principles in the law mentioned in s 240 (whether or not on just terms).
-- (4): otherwise, if there is a compulsory acquisition law for the Commonwealth or the State or Territory to which the
-- act is attributable, the court "may ... have regard to" its principles.
-- s 49: compensation is payable once for acts that are essentially the same, and compensation under other laws for
-- essentially the same act must be taken into account.
DECLARE `Which compensation rules apply` IS ONE OF
    `just terms for the effect on your native title (s 51(1)); as the act is a compulsory acquisition, the court may have regard to the principles in the acquisition law (s 51(2))`
    `the court must apply the compensation principles of the law under which the similar compensable interest test is met, whether or not on just terms (s 51(3))`
    `just terms for the effect on your native title (s 51(1)); the court may have regard to the principles in the compulsory acquisition law of the Commonwealth or the State or Territory (s 51(4))`
    `just terms for the effect on your native title (s 51(1)); no other law's principles are named`

@export On what basis will compensation for an act affecting our native title be worked out: just terms, or another law's compensation principles (Native Title Act 1993 s 51(1)-(4))?
GIVEN `the act is a compulsory acquisition of our native title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act is the compulsory acquisition of all or any of your native title rights and interests
      `the similar compensable interest test is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the similar compensable interest test is satisfied for the act (s 240: compensation would be payable under another law if you held ordinary title to the land instead)
      `there is a compulsory acquisition law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a compulsory acquisition law for the Commonwealth, State or Territory to which the act is attributable
GIVETH A `Which compensation rules apply`
`s 51 -- which compensation rules apply` `the act is a compulsory acquisition of our native title` `the similar compensable interest test is met` `there is a compulsory acquisition law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the act is a compulsory acquisition of our native title`
        THEN `just terms for the effect on your native title (s 51(1)); as the act is a compulsory acquisition, the court may have regard to the principles in the acquisition law (s 51(2))`
        IF `the similar compensable interest test is met`
        THEN `the court must apply the compensation principles of the law under which the similar compensable interest test is met, whether or not on just terms (s 51(3))`
        IF `there is a compulsory acquisition law`
        THEN `just terms for the effect on your native title (s 51(1)); the court may have regard to the principles in the compulsory acquisition law of the Commonwealth or the State or Territory (s 51(4))`
        OTHERWISE `just terms for the effect on your native title (s 51(1)); no other law's principles are named`

-- s 51A(1): "The total compensation payable under this Division for an act that extinguishes all native title in
-- relation to particular land or waters must not exceed the amount that would be payable if the act were instead a
-- compulsory acquisition of a freehold estate in the land or waters." (2): "This section has effect subject to section
-- 53". s 53(1): where an act would otherwise acquire property other than on just terms, "the person is entitled to such
-- compensation, or compensation in addition to any otherwise provided by this Act, ... as is necessary to ensure that the
-- acquisition is made on paragraph 51(xxxi) just terms". So the cap is the freehold amount, raised to the just terms
-- amount where s 53 requires more (fork F8). For an act that does not extinguish all native title, s 51A sets no cap: a
-- scope limit with no "only", NOTHING.
@export What is the most compensation payable for an act that extinguishes all our native title in particular land or waters (Native Title Act 1993 ss 51A, 53)? The cap is what would be paid for a compulsory acquisition of freehold, unless just terms require more. No cap under s 51A if not all native title is extinguished.
GIVEN `the act extinguishes all native title in the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act extinguishes all native title in the particular land or waters
      `the freehold acquisition amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The compensation (in dollars) that would be payable if the act were instead a compulsory acquisition of a freehold estate in the land or waters
      `the just terms amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The total compensation (in dollars) needed for the acquisition to be on just terms under s 53 and the Constitution s 51(xxxi), if a court has found that more is needed; otherwise 0
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 51A -- the most compensation for extinguishing all native title` `the act extinguishes all native title in the land` `the freehold acquisition amount` `the just terms amount` MEANS
    IF `the act extinguishes all native title in the land`
    THEN JUST (IF `the just terms amount` GREATER THAN `the freehold acquisition amount` THEN `the just terms amount` ELSE `the freehold acquisition amount`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 51(5): "Subject to subsection (6), the compensation may only consist of the payment of money." (6): on a request that
-- compensation be by transfer of property or provision of goods or services, the court must consider it and may instead
-- recommend that the person liable do so within a specified period. (7): if the recommendation is not complied with, the
-- person claiming may ask for money instead. (8): if it is complied with, that is full compensation.
DECLARE `Can our compensation be other than money` IS ONE OF
    `money only: compensation may only be the payment of money unless you ask for property, goods or services (s 51(5), the text's no)`
    `the court must consider your request, and may recommend property, goods or services instead of money (s 51(6))`
    `the recommendation was complied with: the property, goods or services are full compensation (s 51(8))`
    `the recommendation was not complied with: you may ask that the compensation be paid in money instead (s 51(7))`
    `waiting: the period the recommendation specified has not ended (s 51(6)(b))`

@export Can our compensation be given as land, other property, goods or services instead of money, and what if a recommendation to do that is not followed (Native Title Act 1993 s 51(5)-(8))?
GIVEN `we asked for non-money compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have asked that all or part of the compensation be a transfer of property or the provision of goods or services
      `a recommendation was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court (or other body) recommended that the person liable transfer property or provide goods or services within a specified period
      `it was complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person liable did what the recommendation said
      `the period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the period the recommendation specified has ended
GIVETH A `Can our compensation be other than money`
`s 51(5)-(8) -- can our compensation be other than money` `we asked for non-money compensation` `a recommendation was made` `it was complied with` `the period has ended` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `we asked for non-money compensation`)
        THEN `money only: compensation may only be the payment of money unless you ask for property, goods or services (s 51(5), the text's no)`
        IF (NOT `a recommendation was made`)
        THEN `the court must consider your request, and may recommend property, goods or services instead of money (s 51(6))`
        IF `it was complied with`
        THEN `the recommendation was complied with: the property, goods or services are full compensation (s 51(8))`
        IF `the period has ended`
        THEN `the recommendation was not complied with: you may ask that the compensation be paid in money instead (s 51(7))`
        OTHERWISE `waiting: the period the recommendation specified has not ended (s 51(6)(b))`
